meta {
  name: 6d. Add the STA API
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:id
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{sqlDataSetId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "namedApis": [
      { "name": "Things", "slug": "things", "standard": "STA", "version": "1.1" }
    ]
  }
}

tests {
  test("STA API added", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.body.namedApis).to.have.lengthOf(1);
  });
}

docs {
  **SQL saga step 6d** — Add the dataset's STA named API.

  An STA API can be added only while the dataset has an active FROST DataSink, so this step runs
  after step 6b and not with the dataset create in step 5.

  **Precondition:** `sqlDataSetId` is set (step 5); the FROST DataSink of step 6b exists.

  **Expected Response:** 200 OK, `namedApis` holds the `things` (STA) entry.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | NamedApi row created for the dataset |
  | Config Adapter | — (the route is provisioned when the dataset is released) |
  | External System | — |
}
